    "body": "## Why\n\n`init_model_with_meta_device` is an optional override with three meanings: `True` enables meta initialization, `False` disables it, and omission or `None` preserves the provider setting. The construction path currently checks the override's truthiness. That ignores explicit `False` and chooses the construction device directly from the override. The provider configuration and the actual construction context can therefore disagree.\n\nThe distinction is used by model construction and checkpoint/export consumers that request real CPU or GPU tensors. This follows the CPU-initialization override contract already merged in #5925.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Update the provider only when `init_model_with_meta_device is not None`.\n- Select the construction context from the resulting provider value. Enable `torch.device(\"meta\")` when that value is true and retain the caller's context otherwise.\n- Apply the same behavior through direct `get_model` calls and `provide_distributed_model`, whose existing forwarding remains the single path into construction.\n- Document the tri-state contract on both public entry points and `GetModelKwargs`.\n- Cover omission, explicit `None`, and both boolean overrides using the existing model-instantiation regression, including restoration of the surrounding device context.\n\nThe provider value remains the authoritative configuration for later allocation and wrapping stages. ModelProviderMixin's existing deprecation and its replacement API are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nMerged main at `4778c23cc495adc78536be95f23964b13abfddb4`; the current PR head is `11563af2ec6b3aa22069d61d0619f7d0a4648937`. The source-loaded CPU regression was rerun on this head with macOS arm64, Python 3.12.14, and PyTorch 2.14.1: all 12 combinations across both entry points passed. It executed the production `ModelProviderMixin` and `get_model` definitions, used real CPU and meta tensor construction at the construction callback, and checked that the outer CPU context was restored. The earlier `6585f50ab` run passed the same matrix and project pre-commit checks; `git diff --check` passed after the current merge.\n\nThe existing regression is available through the project's Python 3.12 environment:\n\n```bash\nuv run python -m pytest -q \\\n  tests/unit_tests/models/test_model_instantiation.py::TestGetModel::test_meta_initialization_override\n```\n\nThe current-head CPU result isolates the construction boundary with controlled imports and a construction callback; the complete Transformer Engine/DDP construction pipeline remains unverified. The current PR's NVIDIA test matrix needs authorization for the updated head; DCO success alone is not runtime validation.\n\n### Earlier mainline validation\nmerged `0968a32f` into `e4d9a9e3` on 2026-10-13.\n\nall 12 source-loaded cpu/meta cases passed across omitted, null, enabled and disabled overrides through both entry points. the complete pre-commit checks passed. the submodule checkout follows the new mainline pin. the cpu cases load the current provider definitions with controlled dependencies, so full transformer-engine and distributed integration remain outside this local run.\n\n### October 19 mainline integration\n\nMerged `7bd66ba0001d` into `ee7b9f1eb44d` through a normal merge, retaining the complete contribution.\n\nAll 12 current-source CPU/meta construction-boundary cases passed across both public entry points, covering omitted and null overrides, explicit true/false overrides, and restoration of the surrounding device context. Current main passed six and failed six cases. Scoped Ruff 0.9.9 checks passed. The production provider definitions execute with controlled dependencies and a tensor-construction callback; the full Transformer Engine/DDP construction pipeline remains unrun. The Megatron-Core checkout follows the new mainline submodule pin.\n\nProject CI: Please authorize the current-head NVIDIA test matrix and run both public construction entry points through the full Transformer Engine/DDP setup. The CPU/meta construction-boundary results above are ready for review.\n\n",
